There are plenty of YASDs which no quantity of AoLSs will
prevent. Aside from the obvious (removing the AoLS by mistake, or to
use magical breathing, and then forgetting to put it back on before
you need it), there are ill-advised deliberate self-polys (e.g. to
gobble rings), misadventures involving water or lava, and probably
others I'm forgetting.

You can also put all your spare AoLS-s in BoH named "A", then press
the wrong key and put *that* in BoH named "B". Ask me how I know this.
(And yes, I'm the same fool who posted the tale of woe about the BoH
and /oCancel in this very forum, not a week ago.)

Not all of these are "instakills" in the sense of single-turn DYWYPI?,
but they are things that will, at a minimum, negate the profit from
your past mumble turns of farming and then some. If nethack is good at
one thing, it's punishing hubris. You'll get about to the 'v' sound in
"Hah! I'm invulnerable!" before it smacks you down.

Remember, we're talking about blunders here -- stupid actions nobody
would ever deliberately do. Yes, the odds per move are tiny, but (at
least if you're me) they get overwhelming when you're talking about
10^6 moves.

If you're not me, and can play indefinitely with neither error nor
boredom, then hey, farm away.

